# Website & App Builder Agent

A free, local-first AI website and app builder that turns a short natural-language prompt into a generated app spec and a simple preview UI.

This project uses:
- Backend: FastAPI
- Frontend: React + Vite
- Free public APIs: Open-Meteo and OpenStreetMap/Nominatim
- Local AI option: Ollama (optional)

It is designed to work without paid APIs and can run fully on your machine.

## Features
- Build landing pages, SaaS dashboards, portfolios, mini apps, and blog templates
- Detect app type from plain English prompt
- Use public free APIs for city and weather enrichment
- Generate a preview response on the frontend
- Optional integration with local Ollama models for AI-generated copy

## Project structure

```text
website-app-builder-agent/
├── backend/
│   ├── main.py
│   └── requirements.txt
├── frontend/
│   ├── package.json
│   ├── vite.config.js
│   ├── index.html
│   └── src/
│       ├── App.jsx
│       ├── main.jsx
│       └── index.css
├── .gitignore
├── README.md
└── start.sh
```

## Quick start

### 1) Backend

```bash
cd backend
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
```

### 2) Frontend

Open a second terminal:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:5173
```

## API endpoints

### Health

```bash
curl http://localhost:8000/api/health
```

### Build app

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/build \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"prompt":"Create a modern fintech landing page for a startup in Lagos","tone":"premium","style":"dark"}'
```

## Optional local AI

If you want to use a local LLM instead of hardcoded templates:

1. Install Ollama: https://ollama.com/
2. Pull a model:

```bash
ollama pull llama3.1
```

3. Edit `backend/main.py` and replace the `generate_copy()` function with calls to the local Ollama API.

## Free APIs used
- Nominatim: geocoding / city lookup
- Open-Meteo: weather data

## Notes
- The app is intentionally easy to extend.
- You can add your own templates or attach a local LLM for richer copy generation.
- This is intentionally built as a lightweight MVP and remains free to run.

